Membrane-Woven Network Eigenmodes: From Uτ=0 to Geometric Derivation of Physical Observables
Second Mathematical Weapon of TDMU
Associated Framework: TDMU · MJP-τ


Abstract
Starting from a set of postulates—namely, that the shared link number density of a woven network on the membrane satisfies an intrinsic equation of state, a continuity equation, and an Euler equation—we derive the linear response equation for small perturbations of the local woven state. We prove that this equation is equivalent to a wave equation with a mass term. By imposing topological boundary conditions on a closed spherical surface and excluding the singularity at the origin, the solution is uniquely discretized into a zero sequence of spherical Bessel functions, yielding a geometric origin for the particle mass spectrum and cosmological expansion dynamics. The entire derivation relies solely on four geometric state variables of the woven network and introduces no external fitting parameters.

